WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00.290 --> 00:06.391
We’ve looked at empathy, and now we are going to explore Purpose, the second part in the EPIC framework.

2
00:06.391 --> 00:10.850
Purpose is really about defining what you want to get out of an interaction.

3
00:11.270 --> 00:17.090
But it’s more than just defining your needs and wants. It’s also taking into consideration the other person’s

4
00:17.540 --> 00:20.144
needs and wants for the interaction as well.

5
00:20.144 --> 00:24.643
And so when we look at defining purpose, we want to define it in three ways.

6
00:24.643 --> 00:31.450
First, we want to explore — given what we understand about how the person is feeling and thinking about the topic —

7
00:31.590 --> 00:35.991
what is realistically achievable in this meeting or in this interaction?

8
00:35.991 --> 00:40.513
Second, we want to take into account: what are our goals for this meeting?

9
00:40.513 --> 00:45.709
And third, we want to look at: what are the other person’s goals for the interaction?

10
00:45.709 --> 00:47.420
And defining purpose in this

11
00:48.130 --> 00:54.210
multifaceted way ensures that we are designing or creating an experience or an interaction

12
00:54.730 --> 00:58.790
that is genuinely inclusive and is a two-way conversation —

13
00:59.940 --> 01:02.850
that it’s not just about transmitting

14
01:03.240 --> 01:11.070
your needs, your ideas only in a one-way fashion, but creating a dialogue and building that relationship over the longer term.

